<title>SOUTH AFRICA: E Dagga Q1 pre-tax, debenture income falls.</title>
<headline>E Dagga Q1 pre-tax, debenture income falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net income pre-tax and debenture interest</p>
<p>					  13.09	vs 16.02</p>
<p>- Daggafontein plant:</p>
<p>Material treated (tonnes)</p>
<p>				    4,288,000 vs 4,257,000</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)		1,043 vs 1,029</p>
<p>- Withok Dam material - Ergo plant:</p>
<p>Material treated (tonnes)</p>
<p>				    2,126,000 vs 2,063,000</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)		  382 vs 367</p>
<p>- 6L13 PGM Project:</p>
<p>Material treated (tonnes)</p>
<p>					  5,705 vs 5,883</p>
<p>    PGM's produced (troy oz)    9,942 vs 6,214</p>
<p>Full name: East Daggafontein Mines Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said they were continuing to evaluate a number of projects that might be suitable for acquisition.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
